# Never use fake screens

Playwright tests and agents must use the **live Clari5 application** only.

Heal helpers that inject sample HTML (`healEnsure*Shell`, `HEAL-*` rows, “Sample Mobile Number”, Figma mock grids) are **forbidden as a fallback**. If live UI is missing or locators do not match, **fail or Blocked** — do not draw a fake page.

## Must

- Navigate to the real module URL under `BASE_URL` (for example `/kyc/reference-data-registry/instruments`).
- Wait for live chrome (sidebar, tabs, real grid columns such as ENROLLMENT ID).
- If the live grid is not there, throw; leave the product defect or environment blocker visible.

## Must not

- Call `healEnsureRdrMasterShell` or any helper that replaces the DOM with sample rows.
- Overlay a fake screen on top of live Clari5 because `.rdr-layout` / `#tab-mb-mobile` / `MB ID` were missing.
- Assert masking, SLA, or WCAG against heal/sample text.

Figma HTML and heal helpers may be read as reference only. They must never become the page under test.
